      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to set up a system of equations based on the given information.\n\nLet's denote:\n- \\( n \\) as the number of nickels,\n- \\( d \\) as the number of dimes,\n- \\( q \\) as the number of quarters.\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know two things:\n1. The total number of coins is the same in all three types (nickels, dimes, and quarters).\n2. The total value of the coins is $13.20.\n\nWe can write these statements as equations:\n\\[ n + d + q \\]\nThe value of these coins in dollars is:\n\\[ 0.05n + 0.10d + 0.25q = 13.20 \\]\n\nFirst, we need to find the total value of the coins in dollars and convert it to cents:\n\\[ 0.05 \\times n + 0.10 \\times d + 0.25 \\times q = 1320 \\]\n\nSince we have three equations but four unknowns, we must simplify the problem by making some assumptions or eliminating one variable. Let's assume that \\( n = d = q \\):\n\n\\[ n + n + n = 3n \\]\n\n\\[ 0.05n + 0.10n + 0.25n = 1320 \\]\n\nCombine the constants:\n\\[ (0.05 + 0.10 + 0.25)n = 1320 \\]\n\\[ (0.40)n = 1320 \\]\n\\[ n = \\frac{1320}{0.40} \\]\n\\[ n = 3300 \\]\n\nFinally, since \\( n = d = q \\), we conclude that Jamie has 3300 nickels.\n\nTherefore, the solution is:\n\\[ \\boxed{3300} \\]",
